1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:01,333
Your phone rings.

2
00:00:01,733 --> 00:00:05,553
You look at the number and think, "Oh no, is it the bank again?"

3
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:08,293
Forty calls, fifty calls in a day.

4
00:00:08,713 --> 00:00:10,453
Then the WhatsApp messages start.

5
00:00:10,893 --> 00:00:11,693
"Pay today."

6
00:00:11,693 --> 00:00:13,093
"Our person is coming to your house."

7
00:00:13,293 --> 00:00:14,553
"We'll file a police case."

8
00:00:14,993 --> 00:00:18,533
After a point, even the ringtone makes you tense, doesn't it?

9
00:00:19,053 --> 00:00:21,773
You are sitting with your family, but your mind is somewhere else.

10
00:00:22,173 --> 00:00:23,453
"What if they call my office?

11
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:25,313
What if my family finds out?"

12
00:00:25,633 --> 00:00:28,193
Even at night, these thoughts keep coming back.

13
00:00:28,193 --> 00:00:31,473
If this sounds like your situation, take a moment.

14
00:00:32,133 --> 00:00:32,973
Take a deep breath.

15
00:00:33,393 --> 00:00:34,773
Let's talk about it calmly.

16
00:00:35,173 --> 00:00:38,833
When you can't pay your credit card bill, what can the bank actually do?

17
00:00:39,153 --> 00:00:40,053
What are your rights?

18
00:00:40,413 --> 00:00:41,693
How do you handle the calls?

19
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:43,273
Can you ask for a settlement?

20
00:00:43,793 --> 00:00:46,013
And later, can you improve your credit score?

21
00:00:46,473 --> 00:00:49,313
We'll go through all of this, one step at a time.

22
00:00:49,573 --> 00:00:51,593
You don't need to know difficult banking words.

23
00:00:51,813 --> 00:00:53,313
I'll explain them as we go.

24
00:00:53,693 --> 00:00:59,853
First, one thing must be clear.

25
00:00:59,853 --> 00:01:03,333
If you have the money to pay, paying on time is better.

26
00:01:03,773 --> 00:01:07,973
This video is for people who are trying to pay but cannot manage it right now.

27
00:01:08,253 --> 00:01:09,573
Maybe your salary has stopped.

28
00:01:09,953 --> 00:01:12,253
Maybe someone at home needed hospital treatment.

29
00:01:12,693 --> 00:01:17,173
Maybe you are using one card to pay another, and now the bills have become too much.

30
00:01:17,693 --> 00:01:21,664
Saying, "I have money, but I'll not pay," and saying, "I want to pay,

31
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:24,713
but I can't manage it now," are different situations.

32
00:01:25,053 --> 00:01:27,333
So first, be honest with yourself.

33
00:01:27,673 --> 00:01:29,233
How much can you really afford?

34
00:01:29,233 --> 00:01:31,833
Usually, the problem starts small.

35
00:01:32,253 --> 00:01:33,293
A hospital bill comes.

36
00:01:33,673 --> 00:01:34,513
A job is lost.

37
00:01:34,873 --> 00:01:36,673
A customer does not pay you on time.

38
00:01:36,993 --> 00:01:38,853
You think, "Let me use the card now.

39
00:01:39,093 --> 00:01:40,453
Next month, I'll clear it."

40
00:01:40,613 --> 00:01:42,853
But next month, another expense comes.

41
00:01:43,173 --> 00:01:45,053
So you arrange money from another card.

42
00:01:45,413 --> 00:01:47,433
Then you pay only the minimum due.

43
00:01:47,773 --> 00:01:49,253
After that, a small loan.

44
00:01:49,613 --> 00:01:51,093
Then a loan from an app.

45
00:01:51,453 --> 00:01:55,373
Your salary comes, and within a few days, almost everything is gone.

46
00:01:55,733 --> 00:01:58,333
You sit there wondering, "I am earning money.

47
00:01:58,333 --> 00:02:00,273
Then why am I always short?"

48
00:02:00,713 --> 00:02:01,713
Does that sound familiar?

49
00:02:02,213 --> 00:02:04,153
Let's stop and ask one question.

50
00:02:04,473 --> 00:02:09,073
If we keep taking new loans to pay old loans, is the total debt coming down?

51
00:02:09,073 --> 00:02:11,973
Or are we only moving the problem to next month?

52
00:02:12,293 --> 00:02:13,813
It is not an easy question.

53
00:02:14,053 --> 00:02:17,633
But answering it honestly helps you see what needs to change.

54
00:02:17,993 --> 00:02:19,373
And please remember this.

55
00:02:19,693 --> 00:02:22,093
Having debt does not make you a bad person.

56
00:02:22,393 --> 00:02:24,993
Being late with a bill does not decide your value.

57
00:02:25,313 --> 00:02:26,753
You have a money problem.

58
00:02:26,753 --> 00:02:28,313
A serious one, yes.

59
00:02:28,633 --> 00:02:31,933
But it needs a plan, support, and the right information.

60
00:02:32,353 --> 00:02:33,873
Shame will not pay the bill.

61
00:02:34,353 --> 00:02:36,493
And panic will not help you choose well.

62
00:02:37,033 --> 00:02:38,333
So, where do you start?

63
00:02:38,853 --> 00:02:40,693
Start with the needs of your home.

64
00:02:41,173 --> 00:02:41,973
Food.

65
00:02:41,973 --> 00:02:42,773
Rent.

66
00:02:42,773 --> 00:02:43,573
Medicines.

67
00:02:43,713 --> 00:02:45,053
Your children's school expenses.

68
00:02:45,493 --> 00:02:47,513
The basic things your family needs.

69
00:02:47,993 --> 00:02:50,651
Imagine paying someone just to stop the calls,

70
00:02:50,651 --> 00:02:53,193
and then having no money left for medicines.

71
00:02:53,693 --> 00:02:54,613
Will that plan work?

72
00:02:54,613 --> 00:02:57,393
First, write down your monthly income.

73
00:02:57,873 --> 00:03:00,393
Then write down these necessary expenses.

74
00:03:00,893 --> 00:03:04,453
After that, see how much is actually left for repayment.

75
00:03:04,633 --> 00:03:06,473
Put it on paper or in your phone.

76
00:03:06,773 --> 00:03:08,633
Don't keep doing the maths in your head.

77
00:03:08,973 --> 00:03:12,153
When you can see the numbers, you can make a proper decision.

78
00:03:12,713 --> 00:03:15,353
"Somehow, I'll manage" sounds hopeful.

79
00:03:15,713 --> 00:03:18,893
But knowing what you can afford is much more useful.

80
00:03:19,313 --> 00:03:23,967
Now, let us come to the biggest fear.

81
00:03:24,347 --> 00:03:28,087
"If I can't pay my credit card bill, will the police arrest me?"

82
00:03:28,347 --> 00:03:31,504
When someone cannot pay because of genuine money problems,

83
00:03:31,504 --> 00:03:35,207
the issue is generally about recovering the money through civil law.

84
00:03:35,587 --> 00:03:39,467
Missing a payment, by itself, doesn't automatically mean cheating.

85
00:03:39,887 --> 00:03:42,127
A cheating case depends on the facts.

86
00:03:42,527 --> 00:03:44,527
Was there a dishonest plan from the beginning?

87
00:03:44,967 --> 00:03:46,347
Were fake documents used?

88
00:03:46,647 --> 00:03:48,547
Was someone deliberately misled?

89
00:03:48,867 --> 00:03:50,507
Those are separate questions.

90
00:03:50,927 --> 00:03:53,865
The Supreme Court has also explained that breaking a

91
00:03:53,865 --> 00:03:57,707
payment agreement and cheating are not automatically the same thing.

92
00:03:57,927 --> 00:03:59,094
So a caller shouting,

93
00:03:59,094 --> 00:04:02,987
"We'll put a criminal case on you," does not decide what the law says.

94
00:04:03,327 --> 00:04:06,167
But please don't take this to mean, "Nothing can happen,

95
00:04:06,167 --> 00:04:07,587
so I can ignore everything."

96
00:04:07,887 --> 00:04:09,867
The bank can send a legal notice.

97
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:11,647
It can start a recovery case.

98
00:04:11,947 --> 00:04:15,347
It can use the legal process that applies to your account.

99
00:04:15,607 --> 00:04:18,347
And a court order can have serious consequences.

100
00:04:19,187 --> 00:04:24,049
If you receive a real legal notice, court summons, or arbitration notice,

101
00:04:24,049 --> 00:04:26,047
check it and respond properly.

102
00:04:26,307 --> 00:04:29,967
If you need help, speak to a lawyer or ask about legal aid.

103
00:04:30,387 --> 00:04:34,027
What matters is the actual document and the actual case.

104
00:04:34,587 --> 00:04:36,847
A loud voice on the phone is not proof.

105
00:04:37,347 --> 00:04:39,847
Now you may ask, "What about a cheque that bounced?

106
00:04:39,847 --> 00:04:41,687
Or an auto-debit that failed?"

107
00:04:42,307 --> 00:04:44,487
These can raise separate legal issues.

108
00:04:44,887 --> 00:04:49,216
The answer depends on the payment, the instructions you gave, the notice,

109
00:04:49,216 --> 00:04:50,047
and the facts.

110
00:04:50,527 --> 00:04:53,073
Don't assume that no other law can apply just

111
00:04:53,073 --> 00:04:55,847
because the original bill was from a credit card.

112
00:04:56,167 --> 00:04:56,967
Read the notice.

113
00:04:57,307 --> 00:04:58,267
Check what it says.

114
00:04:58,647 --> 00:05:00,167
Get advice when needed.

115
00:05:00,687 --> 00:05:06,453
Another common worry is, "I have dues with four or five banks.

116
00:05:06,753 --> 00:05:08,273
How do I handle all of them?"

117
00:05:08,993 --> 00:05:10,853
One call ends, and another starts.

118
00:05:12,173 --> 00:05:15,673
Sometimes, you can't even remember the exact balance on each card.

119
00:05:16,153 --> 00:05:17,753
So make one simple list.

120
00:05:18,093 --> 00:05:22,299
For each card, write the bank's name, the amount due, the due date,

121
00:05:22,299 --> 00:05:23,993
and your last payment date.

122
00:05:23,993 --> 00:05:27,453
Add any complaint number or legal notice you have received.

123
00:05:27,913 --> 00:05:29,933
Keep each account's papers together.

124
00:05:30,293 --> 00:05:30,773
That way,

125
00:05:30,773 --> 00:05:35,993
you are looking at facts instead of trying to remember everything while someone is pressuring you.

126
00:05:36,413 --> 00:05:39,553
Also, settling one card does not settle the others.

127
00:05:39,993 --> 00:05:42,093
Each account needs its own attention.

128
00:05:42,613 --> 00:05:46,553
And don't assume, "My amount is small, so this bank will never go to court."

129
00:05:46,973 --> 00:05:50,509
The bank's decision can depend on the account, its own policy,

130
00:05:50,509 --> 00:05:52,333
and the legal options available.

131
00:05:52,333 --> 00:05:56,413
Build your plan around checking and answering real communication.

132
00:05:56,773 --> 00:06:00,753
Don't build it around guesses about what the bank will or will not do.

133
00:06:01,213 --> 00:06:05,173
Now, open your statement.

134
00:06:05,653 --> 00:06:08,013
Have you ever thought, "I stopped using the card.

135
00:06:08,233 --> 00:06:09,393
They even blocked it.

136
00:06:09,533 --> 00:06:11,613
Then why is the balance still increasing?"

137
00:06:12,213 --> 00:06:14,433
Blocking the card may stop new purchases.

138
00:06:14,933 --> 00:06:17,543
It doesn't automatically stop interest or other

139
00:06:17,543 --> 00:06:19,653
charges that apply to the old balance.

140
00:06:20,073 --> 00:06:22,333
So don't look only at the final total.

141
00:06:22,693 --> 00:06:24,293
Check what is inside it.

142
00:06:24,293 --> 00:06:26,213
How much did you actually spend?

143
00:06:26,513 --> 00:06:27,433
How much is interest?

144
00:06:27,813 --> 00:06:29,353
How much is the late payment fee?

145
00:06:29,653 --> 00:06:30,453
What are the taxes?

146
00:06:30,873 --> 00:06:32,813
And where did your earlier payments go?

147
00:06:33,293 --> 00:06:36,113
Ask for a clear breakdown if you don't understand.

148
00:06:36,533 --> 00:06:37,553
Let's take an example.

149
00:06:38,013 --> 00:06:39,613
Suppose you owe one lakh rupees.

150
00:06:39,993 --> 00:06:42,320
If the monthly interest rate is three percent,

151
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:45,253
that works out to about three thousand rupees in interest.

152
00:06:45,653 --> 00:06:46,973
This is just an example.

153
00:06:47,293 --> 00:06:50,233
Your card's actual rate and calculation can be different.

154
00:06:50,473 --> 00:06:51,533
Check your own terms.

155
00:06:51,533 --> 00:06:54,693
Now add any fees and taxes that apply.

156
00:06:55,033 --> 00:06:56,420
If your payment is small,

157
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:59,693
very little may go towards the amount you originally spent.

158
00:07:00,113 --> 00:07:04,073
That is why you may feel, "I keep paying, but the bill is not coming down."

159
00:07:04,513 --> 00:07:06,433
Let's also clear up the minimum due.

160
00:07:06,833 --> 00:07:09,993
Paying that small amount does not clear your full bill.

161
00:07:10,473 --> 00:07:13,073
Interest may continue on the balance left unpaid.

162
00:07:13,493 --> 00:07:17,473
Depending on your card's terms, you may also lose the interest-free benefit.

163
00:07:17,873 --> 00:07:20,313
But the minimum due is not useless either.

164
00:07:20,313 --> 00:07:25,313
Paying the required minimum on time can help stop the account from becoming overdue.

165
00:07:25,533 --> 00:07:30,253
The difficulty comes when you keep paying only that amount, month after month.

166
00:07:30,593 --> 00:07:32,933
The debt can stay with you for a long time.

167
00:07:33,213 --> 00:07:36,333
So, if you can afford the full bill, clear it.

168
00:07:36,473 --> 00:07:40,313
If you can't, ask the bank for a repayment option you can manage.

169
00:07:40,733 --> 00:07:43,553
There is an important RBI protection here too.

170
00:07:43,733 --> 00:07:45,083
Unpaid taxes, levies,

171
00:07:45,083 --> 00:07:50,933
and charges must not be added to the principal just to charge or compound interest on them.

172
00:07:51,213 --> 00:07:52,145
In simple words,

173
00:07:52,145 --> 00:07:57,853
these unpaid amounts cannot simply become new borrowing on which the bank keeps charging interest.

174
00:07:58,193 --> 00:08:02,805
Also, when checking whether you crossed your credit limit for an over-limit fee,

175
00:08:02,805 --> 00:08:07,473
the bank must not include interest, taxes, and other charges in that calculation.

176
00:08:07,853 --> 00:08:11,873
If something looks wrong in your statement, ask the bank to explain it in writing.

177
00:08:12,193 --> 00:08:15,673
You don't have to accept a charge only because it appears on the bill.

178
00:08:15,673 --> 00:08:15,899
Now,

179
00:08:15,899 --> 00:08:20,913
does this mean the bank must remove all your interest and fees if you ask for settlement?

180
00:08:21,473 --> 00:08:22,273
No.

181
00:08:22,273 --> 00:08:26,173
The bank may agree to reduce some dues, but that is not guaranteed.

182
00:08:26,593 --> 00:08:30,293
It depends on your situation, the account, and the bank's approval.

183
00:08:30,913 --> 00:08:35,304
Before asking for a settlement, understand the amount you spent, your payments,

184
00:08:35,304 --> 00:08:36,193
and the charges.

185
00:08:36,573 --> 00:08:38,013
Then you know what you are discussing.

186
00:08:38,573 --> 00:08:42,667
Next, check your salary account.

187
00:08:43,047 --> 00:08:46,047
Is it with the same bank where your credit card payment is overdue?

188
00:08:46,047 --> 00:08:49,747
If yes, read the account and card terms carefully.

189
00:08:50,127 --> 00:08:52,087
Look for words like "lien" or "set-off".

190
00:08:53,087 --> 00:08:54,267
These may sound confusing.

191
00:08:54,727 --> 00:08:57,724
The point is this: under the terms and law that apply,

192
00:08:57,724 --> 00:09:01,887
the bank may be able to use money in your account with it to pay your dues.

193
00:09:02,307 --> 00:09:05,307
So don't assume, "The card is separate from my savings account.

194
00:09:05,507 --> 00:09:06,927
My salary cannot be touched."

195
00:09:07,407 --> 00:09:09,667
Some agreements give the bank these rights.

196
00:09:11,067 --> 00:09:14,767
Think ahead about the money you need for rent, food, and medicines.

197
00:09:14,767 --> 00:09:18,427
If needed, get advice about your salary banking arrangement.

198
00:09:18,947 --> 00:09:21,917
But moving your salary to another account does not make

199
00:09:21,917 --> 00:09:25,427
the debt disappear or protect you from every legal recovery step.

200
00:09:25,847 --> 00:09:29,247
You still have to follow valid legal duties and court orders.

201
00:09:29,707 --> 00:09:34,207
The idea here is to understand the risk and plan for your family's basic needs.

202
00:09:34,807 --> 00:09:38,827
Now, how do you talk to the bank?

203
00:09:39,887 --> 00:09:43,747
After so many calls, you may think, "Let me switch off my phone.

204
00:09:44,007 --> 00:09:45,367
I just want some peace."

205
00:09:45,367 --> 00:09:47,507
That feeling is understandable.

206
00:09:47,967 --> 00:09:50,967
But the bank still needs to hear what your situation is.

207
00:09:51,287 --> 00:09:54,527
Instead of only handling calls, explain it in writing.

208
00:09:54,947 --> 00:09:56,567
Open the bank's official website.

209
00:09:56,887 --> 00:10:00,227
Find the grievance officer's or nodal officer's contact details.

210
00:10:00,507 --> 00:10:02,367
These are the bank's complaint contacts.

211
00:10:02,687 --> 00:10:05,687
Send an email explaining why payment has become difficult.

212
00:10:06,027 --> 00:10:07,167
You don't need big words.

213
00:10:07,387 --> 00:10:09,487
You can say, "My income has come down.

214
00:10:09,707 --> 00:10:11,407
I have medical expenses at home.

215
00:10:11,687 --> 00:10:13,347
I want to discuss a payment plan.

216
00:10:13,767 --> 00:10:17,367
After my basic expenses, this is what I can afford each month."

217
00:10:17,747 --> 00:10:19,667
Simple and honest is enough.

218
00:10:20,107 --> 00:10:22,527
Don't agree to an amount just to end the call.

219
00:10:22,927 --> 00:10:26,287
Saying, "I'll pay tomorrow," may give you a few minutes of peace.

220
00:10:26,567 --> 00:10:30,227
But if the money will not be there tomorrow, the same problem comes back.

221
00:10:30,527 --> 00:10:33,467
You can calmly say, "I can't promise that amount.

222
00:10:33,907 --> 00:10:36,147
Please tell me what other options are available."

223
00:10:36,547 --> 00:10:41,687
Ask about a smaller EMI, a payment plan, a change in repayment terms, or settlement.

224
00:10:42,127 --> 00:10:46,507
Ask which options your account qualifies for, and get the details in writing.

225
00:10:46,787 --> 00:10:49,307
You can ask them to contact you mainly by email.

226
00:10:49,587 --> 00:10:53,747
But that request doesn't automatically stop the bank from making lawful calls.

227
00:10:54,107 --> 00:10:56,246
Your preference for email and your right

228
00:10:56,246 --> 00:10:58,867
to complain about harassment are separate things.

229
00:10:59,307 --> 00:11:03,087
Save the emails, replies, attachments, and complaint numbers.

230
00:11:03,427 --> 00:11:04,687
Keep them in one folder.

231
00:11:05,187 --> 00:11:08,127
Will sending an email automatically stop a legal case?

232
00:11:08,587 --> 00:11:09,387
No.

233
00:11:09,387 --> 00:11:10,867
But it gives you a record.

234
00:11:11,147 --> 00:11:13,949
It shows what you told the bank, what you asked for,

235
00:11:13,949 --> 00:11:16,267
and how you tried to deal with the problem.

236
00:11:16,747 --> 00:11:21,253
Now, let us talk about recovery agents.

237
00:11:21,693 --> 00:11:23,473
They can contact you about payment.

238
00:11:23,733 --> 00:11:27,687
But that does not give them permission to insult you, threaten you,

239
00:11:27,687 --> 00:11:30,873
shame you in public, or disturb your family's privacy.

240
00:11:31,333 --> 00:11:36,121
RBI instructions don't allow threatening or anonymous calls, abusive messages,

241
00:11:36,121 --> 00:11:37,533
or repeated harassment.

242
00:11:37,973 --> 00:11:41,056
Calls for recovering overdue dues must not be made before

243
00:11:41,056 --> 00:11:43,813
eight in the morning or after seven in the evening.

244
00:11:44,033 --> 00:11:48,753
And no, that does not mean they can say anything they like between eight and seven.

245
00:11:49,053 --> 00:11:50,673
The time rule is one rule.

246
00:11:50,993 --> 00:11:52,753
Harassment is still not allowed.

247
00:11:53,253 --> 00:11:55,113
Suppose someone says, "We'll tell your neighbours.

248
00:11:55,873 --> 00:11:57,773
We'll come to your office and embarrass you.

249
00:11:57,913 --> 00:11:59,053
We'll trouble your family."

250
00:11:59,473 --> 00:12:02,013
You don't have to treat this as normal recovery.

251
00:12:02,473 --> 00:12:04,233
Ask calmly, "What is your name?

252
00:12:04,653 --> 00:12:05,893
Which agency are you from?

253
00:12:06,293 --> 00:12:07,733
Which bank are you calling for?

254
00:12:08,073 --> 00:12:11,153
Please send your authorisation details through an official email."

255
00:12:11,353 --> 00:12:13,153
You don't have to match their volume.

256
00:12:13,153 --> 00:12:17,413
The aim is to keep a record and deal with the issue through the right channel.

257
00:12:17,813 --> 00:12:21,533
You can say, "I have already explained my problem to the bank in writing.

258
00:12:21,893 --> 00:12:23,993
I'll discuss payment through the official channel.

259
00:12:24,273 --> 00:12:25,493
Please don't threaten me."

260
00:12:25,613 --> 00:12:26,413
Keep it short.

261
00:12:26,733 --> 00:12:28,733
You don't need to win a shouting match.

262
00:12:29,173 --> 00:12:31,913
What if someone on WhatsApp asks for your live location?

263
00:12:32,873 --> 00:12:33,673
Wait.

264
00:12:33,673 --> 00:12:35,433
Do you know who this person is?

265
00:12:36,173 --> 00:12:38,313
Have you checked that the bank has authorised them?

266
00:12:38,613 --> 00:12:41,433
Don't send your location just because a stranger asks.

267
00:12:41,433 --> 00:12:45,673
Never share your OTP, PIN, password, or card details.

268
00:12:46,133 --> 00:12:49,253
A location request alone does not prove a person is fake.

269
00:12:49,533 --> 00:12:53,153
But you should check their identity before sharing personal information.

270
00:12:53,573 --> 00:12:57,273
Another message says, "We came to your house, but the door was locked."

271
00:12:57,853 --> 00:12:58,653
First, check.

272
00:12:59,053 --> 00:12:59,853
Who came?

273
00:12:59,853 --> 00:13:00,653
When?

274
00:13:00,653 --> 00:13:01,453
From which agency?

275
00:13:01,893 --> 00:13:03,993
Confirm through the bank's official contact.

276
00:13:04,453 --> 00:13:05,853
Some messages may be real.

277
00:13:06,113 --> 00:13:06,913
Some may not.

278
00:13:07,273 --> 00:13:09,313
Fear should not make the decision for you.

279
00:13:09,313 --> 00:13:13,293
And what about, "Click this link to see your legal notice"?

280
00:13:13,873 --> 00:13:15,453
Don't rush to tap an unknown link.

281
00:13:15,933 --> 00:13:20,453
Open the official bank app or website yourself, or call verified customer care.

282
00:13:20,973 --> 00:13:23,951
A legal message can arrive by email or WhatsApp too,

283
00:13:23,951 --> 00:13:26,813
so don't reject it only because of how it arrived.

284
00:13:27,213 --> 00:13:31,373
Check who sent it, the case details, and any court or lawyer information.

285
00:13:31,833 --> 00:13:35,173
Taking a few minutes to verify is better than clicking in panic.

286
00:13:35,573 --> 00:13:37,913
What if an agent actually comes to your house?

287
00:13:37,913 --> 00:13:39,813
First, stay calm.

288
00:13:40,233 --> 00:13:43,333
If you are uncomfortable, you don't have to invite them inside.

289
00:13:43,733 --> 00:13:46,513
Ask for their ID and the bank's authorisation letter.

290
00:13:46,913 --> 00:13:48,793
Check which account they are visiting about.

291
00:13:49,153 --> 00:13:51,073
Speak in a place where you feel safe.

292
00:13:51,433 --> 00:13:54,793
If you need support, ask someone you trust to stay with you.

293
00:13:55,053 --> 00:13:56,953
Suppose they say, "Sign this now.

294
00:13:57,133 --> 00:13:57,933
Give me cash.

295
00:13:57,953 --> 00:13:58,833
Hand over your phone."

296
00:13:59,253 --> 00:14:01,833
Don't act just because they are pressuring you.

297
00:14:02,013 --> 00:14:03,793
Read any paper before signing.

298
00:14:04,133 --> 00:14:06,593
If you don't understand it, get advice first.

299
00:14:06,593 --> 00:14:10,693
If there is force, a physical threat, or immediate danger, call one one two.

300
00:14:11,753 --> 00:14:13,333
Your safety comes first.

301
00:14:13,693 --> 00:14:14,694
At the same time,

302
00:14:14,694 --> 00:14:18,813
a recovery visit by an authorised person is not automatically illegal.

303
00:14:19,193 --> 00:14:23,193
What matters is how they behave and whether they follow the proper process.

304
00:14:23,573 --> 00:14:26,033
If someone is harassing you, how do you complain?

305
00:14:26,393 --> 00:14:29,693
Keep the dates, times, phone numbers, and messages.

306
00:14:30,153 --> 00:14:32,633
Save screenshots and any evidence you have.

307
00:14:32,953 --> 00:14:36,753
Instead of only saying, "They keep calling," explain what happened.

308
00:14:37,053 --> 00:14:41,193
"This number called on this date, at this time, and said these words."

309
00:14:41,533 --> 00:14:43,073
That makes your complaint clearer.

310
00:14:43,613 --> 00:14:46,773
Send it to the bank's grievance team and ask for a complaint number.

311
00:14:47,173 --> 00:14:50,802
If the bank rejects the complaint, gives an unsatisfactory reply,

312
00:14:50,802 --> 00:14:52,867
or does not reply within thirty days,

313
00:14:52,867 --> 00:14:57,053
you may be able to take it to the RBI Ombudsman under the rules that apply.

314
00:14:57,273 --> 00:15:01,633
This is RBI's process for looking into eligible complaints against banks.

315
00:15:01,893 --> 00:15:08,413
The official Complaint Management System address is cms dot rbi dot org dot in.

316
00:15:08,713 --> 00:15:10,943
One thing to remember: a complaint about

317
00:15:10,943 --> 00:15:13,673
harassment deals with how recovery is being done.

318
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:15,513
It doesn't cancel what you owe.

319
00:15:15,853 --> 00:15:18,513
It also does not guarantee a settlement discount.

320
00:15:18,773 --> 00:15:21,273
But you can ask for fair treatment.

321
00:15:21,653 --> 00:15:27,513
Now, what if constant calls are disturbing your whole day?

322
00:15:27,933 --> 00:15:28,993
Use your phone settings.

323
00:15:29,393 --> 00:15:30,973
Block known abusive numbers.

324
00:15:31,273 --> 00:15:32,473
Turn on spam filters.

325
00:15:32,833 --> 00:15:35,773
WhatsApp also has a Silence Unknown Callers option.

326
00:15:35,773 --> 00:15:38,673
But keep a way for the bank to contact you properly.

327
00:15:38,913 --> 00:15:41,673
Check verified emails and collect official letters.

328
00:15:41,913 --> 00:15:43,653
Also think about your daily needs.

329
00:15:43,993 --> 00:15:47,953
If you silence every unknown caller, you may miss a hospital, job,

330
00:15:47,953 --> 00:15:49,213
or delivery call too.

331
00:15:49,433 --> 00:15:50,853
Choose what works for you.

332
00:15:51,033 --> 00:15:54,773
Set aside a regular time to check bank messages and reply when needed.

333
00:15:55,093 --> 00:15:58,253
You don't have to spend your whole day reacting to every ring.

334
00:15:58,533 --> 00:16:01,613
Will the account close if you stop answering for sixty days?

335
00:16:01,893 --> 00:16:03,253
There is no such guarantee.

336
00:16:03,773 --> 00:16:07,093
One recovery agency may stop calling, and another may start.

337
00:16:07,293 --> 00:16:08,373
The team may change.

338
00:16:08,733 --> 00:16:11,773
The debt does not disappear because the calls become quiet.

339
00:16:12,093 --> 00:16:16,033
Keep working on your budget, written communication, and repayment options.

340
00:16:16,493 --> 00:16:21,240
Now, let us understand the payment timeline.

341
00:16:21,660 --> 00:16:23,240
Your statement has a due date.

342
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:26,480
Pay the full bill or the required minimum by that date.

343
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:29,560
If the full bill is not paid, interest may apply.

344
00:16:29,820 --> 00:16:34,000
If even the full minimum due is not paid, the account becomes overdue.

345
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:38,067
RBI rules say the account must be past due for more than three days

346
00:16:38,067 --> 00:16:42,620
before late payment charges can be added or it can be reported as past due.

347
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:45,680
But the delay is counted from the original due date.

348
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:48,100
Those three days are not a new due date.

349
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:50,100
Don't plan your payment around them.

350
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:54,972
As the delay grows, recovery calls may increase, the bank may restrict the account,

351
00:16:54,972 --> 00:16:57,120
and your credit report may be affected.

352
00:16:57,520 --> 00:17:00,360
Some people think, "Nothing will happen until ninety days."

353
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,100
That is not correct.

354
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:06,700
Charges, overdue reporting, and recovery follow-up can happen earlier.

355
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:08,024
Under RBI rules,

356
00:17:08,024 --> 00:17:13,984
if the statement's minimum amount due is not fully paid within ninety days from the payment due date,

357
00:17:13,984 --> 00:17:16,640
the credit card account is treated as an NPA.

358
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:17,880
What is NPA?

359
00:17:18,260 --> 00:17:20,260
It means Non-Performing Asset.

360
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:21,485
In simple words,

361
00:17:21,485 --> 00:17:26,080
the bank puts the account in a category for payments that have not come in as required.

362
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:29,300
The bank then follows the accounting rules for that category.

363
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:31,380
Does it mean you no longer have to pay?

364
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:32,180
No.

365
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:35,260
The name of the category does not cancel the debt.

366
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:38,440
What if the bank offers to turn your balance into EMIs?

367
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:43,288
Before saying yes, check the monthly payment, interest rate, number of months,

368
00:17:43,288 --> 00:17:45,920
any processing fee, and the total you will pay.

369
00:17:46,220 --> 00:17:49,360
Then ask yourself, "Can I manage this EMI every month?"

370
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:51,580
If it is affordable, it may help.

371
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:52,871
If it is too high,

372
00:17:52,871 --> 00:17:57,660
agreeing just to stop today's pressure may bring the same problem back next month.

373
00:17:58,040 --> 00:17:59,940
Now comes another confusing word: write-off.

374
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:04,620
You hear it and think, "Finally, the bank has removed my debt!"

375
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:06,280
Please check what they mean.

376
00:18:06,820 --> 00:18:10,120
A technical write-off is generally a change in the bank's accounts.

377
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:13,600
It doesn't automatically mean the bank has forgiven your debt.

378
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:15,500
Recovery can still continue.

379
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:18,525
There is also no single rule saying every credit card

380
00:18:18,525 --> 00:18:21,200
must be written off after one hundred and eighty days.

381
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:24,180
The timing can depend on the bank and the account.

382
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:27,500
Waiting for write-off does not guarantee a big discount.

383
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:31,940
If you are struggling now, you can ask the bank about workable options now.

384
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:35,340
You don't have to wait for write-off before asking about settlement.

385
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:40,780
Also, every bank can handle accounts differently.

386
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:45,848
SBI Card, HDFC, ICICI, Axis, YES Bank, Kotak, RBL,

387
00:18:45,848 --> 00:18:49,920
and IDFC FIRST may have different processes.

388
00:18:50,380 --> 00:18:53,340
Even two people with the same bank may get different offers.

389
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:56,020
Your friend says, "I settled by paying only twenty-five percent."

390
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:59,520
That does not mean you will get the same offer.

391
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:03,040
The age of the account, the balance, the person's finances,

392
00:19:03,040 --> 00:19:05,320
and the bank's approval can be different.

393
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:07,100
Check your own written offer.

394
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:10,040
Don't treat an online percentage as a promise.

395
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:13,220
And don't judge an offer only by the caller's tone.

396
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:16,340
A friendly person can still give you wrong information.

397
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:20,380
A rude person is not a reason to ignore real account details.

398
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:21,760
Verify first.

399
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:26,033
So, what is settlement?

400
00:19:26,453 --> 00:19:30,860
The bank agrees to accept an agreed amount that is less than its total claim,

401
00:19:30,860 --> 00:19:33,493
and to waive the rest under agreed conditions.

402
00:19:33,493 --> 00:19:35,513
Both sides have to agree.

403
00:19:35,893 --> 00:19:38,653
Sending your request alone does not make it a settlement.

404
00:19:39,073 --> 00:19:40,673
The bank must approve it.

405
00:19:40,953 --> 00:19:43,233
You can say, "This is what I can arrange now.

406
00:19:43,473 --> 00:19:44,573
I can't promise more.

407
00:19:45,033 --> 00:19:47,393
Please consider a full and final settlement."

408
00:19:47,813 --> 00:19:50,033
Keep the amount and deadline realistic.

409
00:19:50,413 --> 00:19:53,376
If you take another very costly loan to pay the settlement,

410
00:19:53,376 --> 00:19:55,133
have you really solved the problem?

411
00:19:55,573 --> 00:19:57,493
You may have only changed who you owe.

412
00:19:57,913 --> 00:19:59,893
Imagine your balance is one lakh rupees.

413
00:20:00,253 --> 00:20:03,813
A caller says, "Pay thirty thousand rupees, and we'll close everything."

414
00:20:04,193 --> 00:20:05,433
You feel relieved, right?

415
00:20:05,673 --> 00:20:08,993
But before paying, ask for the official settlement letter.

416
00:20:09,273 --> 00:20:12,073
Check the offer through the bank's verified customer care.

417
00:20:12,473 --> 00:20:15,573
A low amount is useful only if the offer is real.

418
00:20:15,853 --> 00:20:20,788
The letter should clearly show your name, account, settlement amount, payment dates,

419
00:20:20,788 --> 00:20:22,433
and any instalment schedule.

420
00:20:22,793 --> 00:20:25,182
What happens to the remaining dues after you

421
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:27,353
pay the agreed amount fully and on time?

422
00:20:27,713 --> 00:20:29,133
Will anything else be claimed?

423
00:20:29,493 --> 00:20:31,713
How will the account appear in your credit report?

424
00:20:31,713 --> 00:20:34,193
Understand these points before paying.

425
00:20:34,593 --> 00:20:39,213
Use an official bank channel or a letter whose authorisation the bank has confirmed.

426
00:20:39,653 --> 00:20:42,173
A WhatsApp screenshot alone is not enough.

427
00:20:42,533 --> 00:20:44,593
If someone says, "Pay a little first.

428
00:20:44,793 --> 00:20:48,713
We'll send the letter later," ask what that payment will count as.

429
00:20:49,033 --> 00:20:50,898
Is it part of the approved settlement,

430
00:20:50,898 --> 00:20:53,253
or just an ordinary payment towards the balance?

431
00:20:53,733 --> 00:20:55,566
You should not discover later that the

432
00:20:55,566 --> 00:20:58,073
bank recorded it differently from what you expected.

433
00:20:58,613 --> 00:21:00,833
Pay only through a method the bank has authorised.

434
00:21:01,213 --> 00:21:05,733
Use its official app, website, or another confirmed payment channel.

435
00:21:06,213 --> 00:21:10,053
Don't send money to an agent's personal UPI account or hand over cash.

436
00:21:10,473 --> 00:21:11,393
Keep the receipt.

437
00:21:11,933 --> 00:21:14,613
If there are instalments, follow the dates carefully.

438
00:21:14,993 --> 00:21:17,453
Ask beforehand what happens if you miss one.

439
00:21:17,933 --> 00:21:19,552
After completing the payments,

440
00:21:19,552 --> 00:21:24,353
get written confirmation and the applicable No Dues or settlement completion certificate.

441
00:21:24,793 --> 00:21:28,373
If a court case is already running, confirm how it will be closed.

442
00:21:28,373 --> 00:21:32,273
"Don't worry, we'll handle it" on a phone call is not enough.

443
00:21:33,753 --> 00:21:35,633
Now, what about Lok Adalat?

444
00:21:36,153 --> 00:21:37,813
Hearing the name may make you nervous.

445
00:21:38,253 --> 00:21:39,293
"Do I have to go to court?

446
00:21:39,633 --> 00:21:40,633
What will they ask me?"

447
00:21:40,953 --> 00:21:44,913
A regular Lok Adalat gives both sides a chance to agree on a settlement.

448
00:21:45,333 --> 00:21:49,653
Eligible disputes can reach it before a case is filed or while a case is pending.

449
00:21:50,053 --> 00:21:51,113
Listen to the offer.

450
00:21:51,313 --> 00:21:52,193
Read the terms.

451
00:21:52,553 --> 00:21:53,873
See whether you can afford them.

452
00:21:54,113 --> 00:21:57,413
You don't have to accept every offer just because you went there.

453
00:21:57,413 --> 00:21:59,773
Agreement from both sides matters.

454
00:22:00,073 --> 00:22:04,857
But once an agreed settlement becomes a Lok Adalat award, it is final and binding,

455
00:22:04,857 --> 00:22:06,373
like a civil court decree.

456
00:22:06,693 --> 00:22:08,313
There is no ordinary appeal.

457
00:22:08,693 --> 00:22:12,953
So don't sign without understanding the amount, dates, and consequences.

458
00:22:13,713 --> 00:22:16,453
Ask, "After I pay this, will anything remain due?

459
00:22:16,893 --> 00:22:18,333
What happens if I miss a payment?

460
00:22:18,673 --> 00:22:20,133
What will my credit report show?"

461
00:22:20,493 --> 00:22:21,953
These are sensible questions.

462
00:22:22,213 --> 00:22:24,333
You have every reason to ask them.

463
00:22:27,120 --> 00:22:29,820
After settlement, another worry comes.

464
00:22:30,160 --> 00:22:31,320
"What about my CIBIL score?

465
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:33,060
Will I ever get a loan again?"

466
00:22:33,540 --> 00:22:35,760
Settlement can affect future approvals.

467
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:38,300
But don't assume your financial life is over.

468
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:42,220
First, understand two words: Settled and Closed.

469
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:46,820
Settled usually means the lender agreed to accept less than the full amount due.

470
00:22:47,180 --> 00:22:50,720
Closed is a different status, usually linked to full repayment.

471
00:22:51,040 --> 00:22:54,400
A lender may view Settled negatively when checking a new application.

472
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:56,497
Getting a No Dues Certificate doesn't

473
00:22:56,497 --> 00:22:59,160
automatically mean your report will say Closed.

474
00:22:59,580 --> 00:23:03,620
The settlement being completed and the credit report status are different things.

475
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:05,340
Can you improve your credit again?

476
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:08,280
Yes, but there is no instant reset.

477
00:23:08,840 --> 00:23:11,840
First, make your income and household budget more stable.

478
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:14,420
Try to build a small emergency fund.

479
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:18,720
You don't need to apply for another card as soon as the old debt is settled.

480
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:23,960
Later, if it suits your situation, you can look at an FD-backed secured card.

481
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:27,000
This is a credit card supported by a fixed deposit.

482
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:31,720
The bank decides whether to approve it, how much deposit is needed, and the limit.

483
00:23:32,280 --> 00:23:34,540
Making an FD does not guarantee approval.

484
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:38,460
And don't lock away all your emergency money just to get a card.

485
00:23:38,840 --> 00:23:42,680
If you get one, use it for small expenses you have already planned.

486
00:23:43,100 --> 00:23:44,900
Pay the full bill by the due date.

487
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:47,280
Keep your use low and affordable.

488
00:23:47,640 --> 00:23:51,972
Using ten or twenty percent of the limit may be one manageable approach,

489
00:23:51,972 --> 00:23:54,980
but no exact percentage guarantees a higher score.

490
00:23:55,260 --> 00:23:56,360
What matters most?

491
00:23:56,840 --> 00:23:58,500
Regular payments on time.

492
00:23:58,760 --> 00:24:00,200
Spending within your means.

493
00:24:00,620 --> 00:24:03,060
Avoiding repeated applications you don't need.

494
00:24:03,580 --> 00:24:05,220
And checking your credit report.

495
00:24:05,580 --> 00:24:08,720
After settlement, see whether the bank has updated it.

496
00:24:08,880 --> 00:24:13,045
If the balance or overdue status is wrong, or an account appears twice,

497
00:24:13,045 --> 00:24:15,860
raise a dispute with the bank and credit bureau.

498
00:24:16,180 --> 00:24:20,360
But correct negative history cannot be removed just because you want it gone.

499
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:22,759
And please be careful with promises like,

500
00:24:22,759 --> 00:24:26,914
"Your score will reach seven hundred and fifty in eighteen months," or,

501
00:24:26,914 --> 00:24:29,840
"Everything will disappear in twenty-four months."

502
00:24:30,360 --> 00:24:32,480
Nobody can promise that for every person.

503
00:24:32,940 --> 00:24:37,020
Your history, current accounts, payments, and reporting all matter.

504
00:24:37,380 --> 00:24:39,560
Focus on habits you can keep following.

505
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:42,840
One difficult period does not decide your whole life.

506
00:24:43,140 --> 00:24:46,361
If you feel scared or don't know how to tell your family,

507
00:24:46,361 --> 00:24:48,000
start with someone you trust.

508
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,780
A family member you feel safe talking to.

509
00:24:51,040 --> 00:24:51,860
A close friend.

510
00:24:52,380 --> 00:24:54,620
You don't have to carry the whole problem alone.

511
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:57,360
You can say, "I am having money problems.

512
00:24:57,760 --> 00:24:58,600
These are my dues.

513
00:24:59,020 --> 00:24:59,860
This is my income.

514
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:01,860
This is the plan I want to follow.

515
00:25:02,420 --> 00:25:03,360
I need some support."

516
00:25:03,880 --> 00:25:06,000
Asking for support is a useful step.

517
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:12,447
Now, let us put everything into eight simple steps.

518
00:25:12,727 --> 00:25:15,547
Step one: list every card and balance.

519
00:25:15,867 --> 00:25:19,347
Write down your income, basic expenses, and repayment money.

520
00:25:19,347 --> 00:25:22,767
Check the terms and any risk to your salary account.

521
00:25:23,007 --> 00:25:27,547
Step two: explain your difficulty through each bank's official complaint channel.

522
00:25:27,787 --> 00:25:29,707
Ask for payment options you can afford.

523
00:25:30,027 --> 00:25:32,227
Save the replies and complaint numbers.

524
00:25:32,687 --> 00:25:35,687
Step three: manage the calls with your phone settings.

525
00:25:36,007 --> 00:25:40,707
But keep checking verified bank emails, letters, and genuine legal notices.

526
00:25:41,187 --> 00:25:45,447
Step four: look carefully at taking new loans to pay old ones.

527
00:25:45,827 --> 00:25:48,647
Understand what minimum payments do and cost.

528
00:25:48,647 --> 00:25:51,387
Don't promise more than your budget allows.

529
00:25:51,647 --> 00:25:55,707
Step five: save evidence of threats or harassment and complain.

530
00:25:56,027 --> 00:25:58,687
Use the RBI complaint process when appropriate.

531
00:25:59,027 --> 00:26:01,087
If you are in immediate danger, call one one two.

532
00:26:02,207 --> 00:26:07,487
Step six: remember that NPA, write-off, and settlement mean different things.

533
00:26:08,247 --> 00:26:09,687
Write-off does not cancel your debt.

534
00:26:09,967 --> 00:26:11,627
Ask about workable options.

535
00:26:12,047 --> 00:26:14,867
Step seven: verify any settlement letter.

536
00:26:14,867 --> 00:26:19,347
Check the amount, dates, remaining-dues waiver, and credit reporting.

537
00:26:19,667 --> 00:26:23,867
Pay through an authorised method and collect receipts and completion confirmation.

538
00:26:24,427 --> 00:26:28,331
Step eight: make your income more stable, build emergency savings,

539
00:26:28,331 --> 00:26:30,047
and check your credit report.

540
00:26:30,347 --> 00:26:34,487
Later, use suitable credit carefully and pay fully on time.

541
00:26:34,887 --> 00:26:37,387
Now ask yourself, "What can I do today?"

542
00:26:38,267 --> 00:26:40,327
You don't need to solve everything today.

543
00:26:40,487 --> 00:26:42,747
But can you take one useful step?

544
00:26:43,127 --> 00:26:44,047
List your accounts.

545
00:26:44,047 --> 00:26:45,527
Check one statement.

546
00:26:45,827 --> 00:26:46,767
Send one email.

547
00:26:47,127 --> 00:26:48,607
Speak to someone you trust.

548
00:26:49,047 --> 00:26:49,847
Start there.

549
00:26:50,027 --> 00:26:52,667
You will have a clearer idea of what to do next.

550
00:26:53,047 --> 00:26:55,927
You owe money, but you still deserve respect.

551
00:26:56,287 --> 00:26:58,187
Be honest about your responsibilities.

552
00:26:58,607 --> 00:26:59,827
Know your rights too.

553
00:27:01,107 --> 00:27:02,687
And I want to share something personal.

554
00:27:03,087 --> 00:27:05,587
I am also dealing with this situation right now.

555
00:27:05,827 --> 00:27:09,187
That is why I understand how tiring this pressure can be.

556
00:27:09,487 --> 00:27:13,787
In the next video, I'll show you my own process: how I speak to the banks,

557
00:27:13,787 --> 00:27:17,507
the letters I send, the replies I get, and the decisions I make.

558
00:27:17,827 --> 00:27:19,427
Your case may turn out differently.

559
00:27:19,747 --> 00:27:23,307
But seeing the process may help you ask better questions about yours.

560
00:27:23,967 --> 00:27:25,287
Subscribe so you don't miss it.

561
00:27:25,407 --> 00:27:27,907
Tap the bell icon and choose All notifications.

562
00:27:28,347 --> 00:27:31,487
If this video helped you, share it with someone who needs it.

563
00:27:31,787 --> 00:27:34,627
They may be going through the same worry without telling anyone.

564
00:27:35,147 --> 00:27:39,407
Your message could help them pause, think clearly, and take their first step.
